uth face from HABS photograph 1, and its two stone stacks\n\nThis PR now ships **T-3107 alone**. That follows the owner's 2026-10-25 handoff: \"finish T-3108, or ship T-3107 alone and leave T-3108 to its ticket\". **T-3108 has been released back to the queue** (`ticket.mjs release`). None of its work was ever built on this branch: the round south-west bay, the narrower paired-light pavilion and the HABS1 camera re-solve.\n\nWhat the PR carries (unchanged from the earlier laps):\n- HABS photograph 1 (Harold Allen, June 1965, from the south-west), ingested with its source record and credit.\n- Its camera, `data/reference_views/kimball_house_1801_prairie/habs_1965_01_southwest.json`, and a match record whose verdict is **DIFFERS** (12 differences open). It does not claim MATCH.\n- The south wall's two tall stacks in pale ashlar, rebaked (K01 frontage params). The rear stack is read off the photograph. The front stack's height is a **ruling, not a reading**: it is held to 18.0 m, the most the c. 1895 Taylor print allows. The 1965 height stays open in both match records and is written up in `L-kimball-1801-south-stacks-3107` in `docs/LIBERTIES.md`.\n- The front-stack height/phase question, the corner cornice residual of about 85 px, and everything that belongs to T-3108, T-3109 and T-3110 are still OPEN, and each is named in the match record.\n\n### This lap\n- Merged `origin/dev` twice, because dev moved during the gate (T-3146, T-3150 and T-3153 landed).\n- `LIBERTIES.md` keeps both sides' entries. `assets/manifest.json` was merged entry by entry with `merge_asset_registry.py`: 33 assets re-emitted, every GLB byte-identical. The derived files were rebuilt with `rederive.mjs --resolve`.\n\n### Verification (foreground, this runner)\n- `./tools/check.sh`: **CHECK PASS, 1068 steps, none red** on the final merged tree (and 1067/1067 on the first merge). No missing-module skips.\n- `check-changelog-entry.mjs` against the merge base: entry present (`changelog.d/T-3107.json`).\n- Smoke, `--published`:\n  - desktop part 3: **SMOKE PASS** (107 assertions).\n  - mobile part 3: **SMOKE PASS** (107 assertions).\n  - desktop part 1: every assertion reached passed, with zero page errors. It did not finish: it ran past the 590 s foreground timeout on this 4-CPU runner (the recorded time is 7 m 13 s on 5 CPUs). CI's own smoke covers the rest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-25T00:40:34Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T15:39:59Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T15:39:53Z","merged_at":"2026-10-25T15:39:53Z","merge_commit_sha":"19fbb127a7332776b9277763a8c7be2ed89e9a7d","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/t3107-t3108-kimball-habs1-corner-camera-20261025","ref":"steward/t3107-t3108-kimball-habs1-corner-camera-20261025","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false